      "id": "Q87",
      "question": "How do you identify a district’s tier on the board, and does being in a higher tier inherently change its production or threat?"
    }

{
      "id": "Q87",
      "expected_answer": "Count the colored bars under its name; this is its tier. District borders also share the color for their tier. Tiers have no inherent effect: printed cards can refer to them, including threat conditions; resource production uses the district’s printed resources and applicable modifiers.",
      "required_facts": [
        "The number of bars under the district name identifies its tier.",
        "Tier has no inherent production/threat effect; printed card instructions can refer to tier."
      ],
      "contextual_background": [
        "Matching district-border color is a supplementary identification aid, not an additional completeness prerequisite."
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "RR20,64,64.1–64.2"
      ]
    }

